{
  "id": "symmetry-channel",
  "title": "A rule reads the symmetry lattice through the $symmetry: channel — ring, antipode, canonical ray, a ring walk, a reflection through another cell, orthogonality, the exact inner product and a projection — and world.symmetry echoes the same maps",
  "binding": "The positive leg boots rows node=5 and mirror=17 and an Edge rule at tick 1 that copies eight $symmetry: reads of 'node' into eight result rows: ring (2), antipode (18), canonicalRay (5), cycle:7 (87 — the same node the state-cycle-trait canary's plane-1 orbit reaches after one step), reflect:cell:mirror (16), orthogonal:17 (0), innerProduct:17 (1 — nodes 5 and 17 are sixty-degree neighbours) and projectionX (0.238006591796875). world.symmetry 5 17 prints the lattice's own answers for the same node and mirror, and they agree line for line, so the channel is the lattice and not a second table. The discriminating leg boots the same rows and the same rule with plain fromState copies of 'node': every result row reads 5 (or 0 for the fixed projection), none of the symmetry values appears, and world.symmetry still answers — the lattice is there, the rule simply never asked it.",
  "bootShape": "headless",
  "requirements": [],
  "seconds": 5,
  "timeoutSeconds": 20,
  "fixtures": [],
  "positive": {
    "world": "tests/Puck.World.Canaries/symmetry-channel/fixture.world.json",
    "script": "positive.script.txt",
    "commands": [
      {
        "verb": "world.status",
        "occurrence": 1,
        "outcome": "accepted"
      },
      {
        "verb": "world.wait",
        "occurrence": 1,
        "outcome": "accepted"
      },
      {
        "verb": "world.state",
        "occurrence": 1,
        "outcome": "accepted"
      },
      {
        "verb": "world.symmetry",
        "occurrence": 1,
        "outcome": "accepted"
